From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devin <devin@cognition.ai>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt/keys: accept qcom,sm8750-tlmm (216 GPIOs)

sm8750 TLMM: compatible qcom,sm8750-tlmm, gpio-ranges <&tlmm 0 0 216>
(mainline sm8750.dtsi). Needed only when gpio-keys reference TLMM pins;
elden's own vol+/vol-/power ride the PMIC path (pm8550_gpios/pon_resin).

CAUTION: the comment above this table warns other SoCs can be multi-tile;
the linear base+gpio*0x1000+4 assumption for sm8750 must be validated on
hardware before relying on any TLMM-referenced input.
---
 src/dt/keys.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/dt/keys.c b/src/dt/keys.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/dt/keys.c
+++ b/src/dt/keys.c
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@ static uint32_t QcomFdtLinearTlmmGpioCount(const void *Blob, int Provider)
   } Layouts[] = {
       {"qcom,sm8450-tlmm", 210U},
       {"qcom,sm8550-tlmm", 210U},
+      {"qcom,sm8750-tlmm", 216U},
   };
   size_t Index;
 
